   "source": [
    "# 02 — Library walkthrough: list Zarr stores and metadata\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the installed **`geoaicubes`** package (editable dev install from this repo) to discover every\n",
    "`*.zarr` store and read **metadata only** (dims, variables, CRS, extent, tile URL templates).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Setup** (repo root):\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "uv sync          # installs geoaicubes in editable mode (same as pip install -e .)\n",
    "jupyter lab notebooks/\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Pick the project `.venv` kernel. Zarr data: `data/GEODATACUBE_ZARR_openEO/` (`config/.env.example`).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "73d41ba0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "geoaicubes 0.1.0 (/home/juan/Desktop/GeoAICubes/src/geoaicubes/__init__.py)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import geoaicubes\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from geoaicubes import __version__\n",
    "from geoaicubes.config import StorageSettings, get_storage_settings\n",
    "from geoaicubes.io import list_zarr_inventory\n",
    "from geoaicubes.io.inventory import discover_store_ids, get_store_inventory\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"geoaicubes {__version__} ({geoaicubes.__file__})\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "49ce9dde",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Storage settings and `discovery_mode`\n",
    "\n",
    "`StorageSettings` (env prefix `GEOAICUBES_STORAGE__`, see `config/.env.example`) controls **how** stores\n",
    "are listed and opened. The main switch is **`discovery_mode`**:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Mode | List stores | Open with Xarray | Inventory `path` | TiTiler `?url=` in templates |\n",
    "|------|-------------|------------------|------------------|-------------------------------|\n",
    "| **`filesystem`** (default) | Scan `local_zarr_root()` for `*.zarr` dirs | On-disk path | Repo-relative path | Absolute filesystem path |\n",
    "| **`s3`** | `s3fs` list under `bucket/prefix/` | S3 mapper | `s3://…` URI | Same `s3://…` URI |\n",
    "\n",
    "Every store record still includes a canonical logical **`uri`** (`s3://bucket/prefix/{id}/`) regardless of mode.\n",
    "\n",
    "Implementation: `src/geoaicubes/config.py`, `src/geoaicubes/io/inventory.py`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "4e70b9b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "{'discovery_mode': 'filesystem',\n",
       " 'local_root': 'data/GEODATACUBE_ZARR_openEO',\n",
       " 'local_zarr_root': '/home/juan/Desktop/GeoAICubes/data/GEODATACUBE_ZARR_openEO',\n",
       " 'zarr_root_exists': True}"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 2,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "settings = get_storage_settings()\n",
    "{\n",
    "    \"discovery_mode\": settings.discovery_mode,\n",
    "    \"local_root\": str(settings.local_root),\n",
    "    \"local_zarr_root\": str(settings.local_zarr_root()),\n",
    "    \"zarr_root_exists\": settings.local_zarr_root().is_dir(),\n",
    "    # \"bucket\": settings.bucket,\n",
    "    # \"prefix\": settings.prefix,\n",
    "    # \"endpoint_url\": settings.endpoint_url,\n",
    "}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0d969743",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Method A — `filesystem`\n",
    "\n",
    "Native dev and current Docker Compose: data lives on disk under `GEOAICUBES_STORAGE__LOCAL_ROOT`.\n",
    "Pass an explicit `StorageSettings` copy so this section does not depend on your `.env` default.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "bdb63497",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "{'count': 6,\n",
       " 'ids': ['GeoDataCube_cobertes-sol-v1r0-2023.zarr',\n",
       "  'Geodatacube_S22024_2025.zarr',\n",
       "  'Geodatacube_nDSM2024.zarr',\n",
       "  'Geodatacube_nDSM2025.zarr',\n",
       "  'Geodatacube_orto2024.zarr',\n",
       "  'Geodatacube_orto2025.zarr'],\n",
       " 'path': 'data/GEODATACUBE_ZARR_openEO/GeoDataCube_cobertes-sol-v1r0-2023.zarr/',\n",
       " 'uri': 's3://data/GEODATACUBE_ZARR_openEO/GeoDataCube_cobertes-sol-v1r0-2023.zarr/',\n",
       " 'tile_url_starts_with': '/tiles/zarr/tiles/WebMercatorQuad/{z}/{x}/{y}.png?url=%2Fhome%2Fjuan%2FDesktop%2'}"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 10,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fs_settings: StorageSettings = settings.model_copy(update={\"discovery_mode\": \"filesystem\"})\n",
    "ids_fs = discover_store_ids(fs_settings)\n",
    "inv_fs = list_zarr_inventory(fs_settings)\n",
    "sample_fs = inv_fs.stores[0]\n",
    "{\n",
    "    \"count\": inv_fs.count,\n",
    "    \"ids\": ids_fs,\n",
    "    \"path\": sample_fs.path,\n",
    "    \"uri\": sample_fs.uri,\n",
    "    \"tile_url_starts_with\": next(iter(sample_fs.tile_url_template.values()))[:80],\n",
    "}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "689f3bee",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Method B — `s3` (MinIO / S3)\n",
    "\n",
    "Requires a running object store (`make minio-up` or Compose), credentials in `.env`, and Zarr prefixes\n",
    "registered under `s3://{bucket}/{prefix}/`. If the bucket layout is empty, listing returns **no stores**\n",
    "(local disk data alone is not enough). See inventory API `status: "error"` payloads and viewer inline errors.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "0a8d325e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "S3 discovery skipped (An HTTP Client raised an unhandled exception: 400, message=\"Bad status line:\\n  Expected HTTP/, RTSP/ or ICE/:\\n\\n  b'\\\\xff\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\x7f'\\n    ^\", url='http://localhost:9000/data?list-type=2&prefix=GEODATACUBE_ZARR_openEO%2F&delimiter=%2F&encoding-type=url'). Start MinIO: make minio-up\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "{'count': 0, 'ids': []}"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 11,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "s3_settings: StorageSettings = settings.model_copy(update={\"discovery_mode\": \"s3\"})\n",
    "ids_s3: list[str] = []\n",
    "s3_connect_error: Exception | None = None\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    ids_s3 = discover_store_ids(s3_settings)\n",
    "except Exception as exc:\n",
    "    s3_connect_error = exc\n",
    "    print(f\"S3 discovery skipped ({exc}). Start MinIO: make minio-up\")\n",
    "\n",
    "s3_summary: dict = {\"count\": 0, \"ids\": []}\n",
    "if ids_s3:\n",
    "    inv_s3 = list_zarr_inventory(s3_settings)\n",
    "    sample_s3 = inv_s3.stores[0]\n",
    "    s3_summary = {\n",
    "        \"count\": inv_s3.count,\n",
    "        \"ids\": ids_s3,\n",
    "        \"path\": sample_s3.path,\n",
    "        \"uri\": sample_s3.uri,\n",
    "        \"status\": sample_s3.status,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "elif s3_connect_error is None:\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        \"No stores under S3 prefix — expected when only disk data is present. \"\n",
    "        f\"Logical layout: s3://{s3_settings.bucket}/{s3_settings.prefix}/\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "s3_summary\n"
   ]
  },
